{
  "contract": "skills-package/v3 — the signature covers the schema",
  "phase": "signature_verification",
  "public_key_b64": "A6EHv/POEL4dcN0Y50vAmWfk1jCbpQ1fHdyGZBJVMbg=",
  "key_note": "The published interoperability key from signing/vectors-v1.json. The seed is disclosed there and must never sign anything real.",
  "note": "`config_schema` lives in `skill.yaml`, so the manifest signature already covers it. These cases prove that placement is load-bearing rather than incidental: a schema an intermediary can widen is a schema that decides nothing.",
  "consumption_note": "Each `manifest` is a complete community package as presented to a loader, carrying a real ed25519 signature over the canonical bytes defined in signing/v1.md. Verify it against `public_key_b64`. Nothing needs composing and no surrounding state needs inventing. `signed_config_schema` records what the author actually signed, for diagnosis only — a consumer never needs it.",
  "ordering_note": "The mutations are deliberately grammar-valid. An invalid one may be refused by schema validation before verification is reached, which is also correct behaviour but proves nothing about whether the signature covers the schema.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "widened_bound_after_signing",
      "manifest": {
        "name": "example-skill",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "author": "example",
        "triggers": [
          {
            "name": "observe",
            "condition": "value > 1",
            "action_tier": "A"
          }
        ],
        "actions": {
          "available": [
            {
              "name": "alert_sms",
              "tier": "A"
            }
          ],
          "defaults": {
            "observe": [
              "alert_sms"
            ]
          }
        },
        "config_schema": {
          "retries": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 99
          }
        },
        "signature": "ed25519:yGwGRzpbBqHYQ+iCQEQfHESSve+gS5OdqFtvKIFbJVxHNo8RNvNw4KnmqEyA8DK8arNqMRHQ7AQ9CRH3CApLCQ=="
      },
      "expect": "refused",
      "error": "SkillSecurityError",
      "signed_config_schema": {
        "retries": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 3
        }
      },
      "why": "A widened bound is the mutation with a motive: it admits configuration the author never agreed to accept, and every value it newly admits is grammar-valid."
    },
    {
      "name": "added_key_after_signing",
      "manifest": {
        "name": "example-skill",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "author": "example",
        "triggers": [
          {
            "name": "observe",
            "condition": "value > 1",
            "action_tier": "A"
          }
        ],
        "actions": {
          "available": [
            {
              "name": "alert_sms",
              "tier": "A"
            }
          ],
          "defaults": {
            "observe": [
              "alert_sms"
            ]
          }
        },
        "config_schema": {
          "retries": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0
          },
          "debug_endpoint": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "signature": "ed25519:E0kwtHr103xfVqtjzT7OZwIjv1tf7eDJSlpNg4JnOo4jjw2hU9ZRSyHXglS5CKyz2zo3goMB+4qtom9TOioKDQ=="
      },
      "expect": "refused",
      "error": "SkillSecurityError",
      "signed_config_schema": {
        "retries": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        }
      },
      "why": "An added key opens a surface the author closed by not declaring it."
    },
    {
      "name": "removed_schema_after_signing",
      "manifest": {
        "name": "example-skill",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "author": "example",
        "triggers": [
          {
            "name": "observe",
            "condition": "value > 1",
            "action_tier": "A"
          }
        ],
        "actions": {
          "available": [
            {
              "name": "alert_sms",
              "tier": "A"
            }
          ],
          "defaults": {
            "observe": [
              "alert_sms"
            ]
          }
        },
        "signature": "ed25519:E0kwtHr103xfVqtjzT7OZwIjv1tf7eDJSlpNg4JnOo4jjw2hU9ZRSyHXglS5CKyz2zo3goMB+4qtom9TOioKDQ=="
      },
      "expect": "refused",
      "error": "SkillSecurityError",
      "signed_config_schema": {
        "retries": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        }
      },
      "why": "Removing the schema is not a way to relax it — absence admits only an empty `config` — but it is still a difference from what was signed, and is refused as one rather than tolerated as harmless."
    },
    {
      "name": "default_changed_after_signing",
      "manifest": {
